+//! is a process of the host's that runs while the shell goes on, with
+//! three of the shell's descriptors as its standard streams: a pipeline's
+//! commands run at once, connected by the host's pipes, and a command
+//! with `&` runs while the shell reads the next line. A stream the host
+//! has no descriptor for (a command substitution's capture) is fed
+//! through a pipe of the host's while the shell waits for the command.
 
